{"format":"vetro-plugin","version":1,"manifest":{"id":"notification-center","name":"Notification Center","version":"0.1.0","apiVersion":1,"permissions":[],"author":"mclaudiopt","description":"Queue notifications from any device on the LAN and show them as native TV banners through a small companion web app. Talks only to Vetro on 127.0.0.1:8099.","main":"index.js","ui":{"label":"Notifications"}},"files":{"README.md":"# Notification Center\n\nAny device on your LAN (PC, phone, script) can `POST` a message to this Shard. It queues the message, asks Vetro to\nlaunch a small companion web app, and the app shows it as a **native Samsung TV banner** (top-right, with the OK /\n\"View history\" buttons, kept in the TV's own notification history). Everything runs on the TV, no PC is needed afterwards.\n\n> **Status: early.** It works end to end on one TV (see \"Tested on\"), but it is **not** a banner on top of the running\n> app: the companion app has to come to the foreground for a few seconds. Read \"Limitations\" before installing.\n\n## Permissions\n\nNone. It does not use `exec`.\n\n## Network\n\n- **Incoming:** HTTP routes under `/plugins/notification-center/api/` (`notify`, `notifications`, `recent`, `config`, `ui`, `nt.js`),\n  open to every device that can reach Vetro, like the rest of Vetro when pairing is off.\n- **Outgoing:** one call, to Vetro itself on `127.0.0.1:8099` (`POST /apps/launch`, body `{\"appId\": \"...\"}`), to start the companion app. At most once every 10 seconds.\n  It talks to no other host and downloads no code.\n\n## Data it keeps\n\n`ctx.config`: `{ \"appId\": \"NotifCtr01.NotifCenter\" }`, the id of the companion app to launch.\nThe queue (up to 5 active notifications) and the list of the last 20 sent are kept in memory only and are cleared when the Shard stops.\n\n## How it works\n\n```\nany device --POST notify--> Shard (queue) --POST /apps/launch--> Vetro launches the companion app\ncompanion app --GET notifications--> Shard      (XHR, or <script> if the TV blocks cross-origin XHR)\ncompanion app --new Notification(title, {body})--> TV banner + TV notification history\ncompanion app stays open ~8 s (it must be on screen for the banner to show), then exits\n```\n\nThe companion app is a **thin loader**: its logic is `nt.js`, served by this Shard, so you can change the logic from the\nVetro panel without reinstalling the app on the TV.\n\n## Install\n\n1. Vetro with root connected. If Vetro keeps restarting, set the TV's **Host PC IP to `127.0.0.1`** (Developer Mode); otherwise\n   it can end up in safe mode (\"Resume plugins\", then restart Vetro).\n2. Install this Shard from the catalog and switch it on.\n3. Build and install the companion app (below) with your own certificate. It needs the privileges `notification` and `internet`.\n4. Send a notification:\n\n```\ncurl -X POST http://<TV-IP>:8099/plugins/notification-center/api/notify \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"title\":\"Oven\",\"message\":\"Dinner is ready\",\"seconds\":30}'\n```\n\nFields: `message` (required, 200 characters), `title` (40), `seconds` (5-300, how long it stays in the queue), `open`\n(`false` only queues it, without launching the app). The page of this Shard (tab **Notifications**) has a form for it.\n\n## The companion app (copy these three files)\n\n`config.xml`\n\n```xml\n<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<widget xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/ns/widgets\" xmlns:tizen=\"http://tizen.org/ns/widgets\" id=\"http://localhost/notifcenter\" version=\"0.1.0\" viewmodes=\"maximized\">\n  <tizen:application id=\"NotifCtr01.NotifCenter\" package=\"NotifCtr01\" required_version=\"6.0\"/>\n  <name>Notification Center</name>\n  <icon src=\"icon.png\"/>\n  <content src=\"index.html\"/>\n  <access origin=\"http://127.0.0.1:8099\" subdomains=\"false\"/>\n  <feature name=\"http://tizen.org/feature/screen.size.all\"/>\n  <tizen:privilege name=\"http://tizen.org/privilege/internet\"/>\n  <tizen:privilege name=\"http://tizen.org/privilege/notification\"/>\n  <tizen:profile name=\"tv-samsung\"/>\n</widget>\n```\n\n`index.html`\n\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Notification Center</title></head>\n<body style=\"background:#0f1218;color:#e8ecf2;font:28px sans-serif;margin:40px\">\n<div id=\"log\"></div>\n<script src=\"js/app.js\"></script>\n</body></html>\n```\n\n`js/app.js` (the loader)\n\n```js\n(function () {\n  \"use strict\";\n  var BASES = [\"http://127.0.0.1:8099\"];\n  var PATH = \"/plugins/notification-center/api/nt.js\";\n  var logEl = document.getElementById(\"log\"), i = 0;\n  function say(t) { var d = document.createElement(\"div\"); d.textContent = t; logEl.appendChild(d); }\n  (function next() {\n    if (i >= BASES.length) { say(\"Could not load nt.js from the Shard. Is it running?\"); return; }\n    var s = document.createElement(\"script\");\n    s.src = BASES[i++] + PATH + \"?t=\" + new Date().getTime();\n    s.onerror = function () { say(\"nt.js failed: \" + s.src.split(\"?\")[0]); next(); };\n    (document.head || document.documentElement).appendChild(s);\n  })();\n})();\n```\n\nAdd any 512x512 `icon.png`, zip the files as `.wgt`, sign it and install it (Apps2Samsung, TV-Store, Tizen Studio).\nIf you use another app id, set it in the **Companion app** box of this Shard's page. If loopback does not answer on your TV,\nadd the TV's own LAN address to `BASES` in `js/app.js` and `nt.js`, and a matching `<access origin=\"...\">` to `config.xml`.\n\n## Limitations (all measured on a real TV)\n\n- **The app must be in the foreground to post.** The web `Notification` API only works while the web app is on screen\n  (a background web app is suspended and its timers stop). So the companion app comes to the front, posts, stays ~8 s\n  (leaving earlier hides the banner), and exits. You will see it for a moment, and what was playing is interrupted briefly.\n- `tizen.notification` / `StatusNotification` **do not exist** on the TV profile; only the web `Notification` API works.\n- **No banner over the running app without launching an app.** I checked that it is not possible from a Shard or a shell:\n  the TV's `libnotification` uses its own sockets (nothing about notifications on the system D-Bus), there is no\n  `notification_test`, and writing to `/opt/dbspace/.notification.db` does not notify the UI. The realistic way is a small\n  background **`service-application`** (native or .NET) with the `notification` privilege calling `NotificationManager.Post`.\n  Nobody has built it here (no Tizen Studio / .NET SDK); **help wanted**.\n- The TV refuses to run **unsigned script files** (\"the file is NOT signed\"); inline commands through Vetro still work. This Shard needs neither.\n- Whether the previous screen comes back cleanly after the app exits was tested only from the launcher, not yet over\n  every kind of source (live TV, HDMI).\n- Anyone who can reach Vetro's port can send notifications and make it launch the app (Vetro without pairing).\n\n## Tested on\n\nSamsung Q70C (TQ55Q70CATXXC), Tizen 9.0, Vetro 0.5.0. The flow (queue, launch, banner top-right, entry in the notification\nhistory, app exits) was tested with an earlier version of this Shard that lived inside another one; this standalone\nversion keeps the same logic and was checked on the TV for its HTTP routes and page.\n","index.js":"'use strict';\n// Notification Center: queue notifications from any device on the LAN and show them as native TV banners\n// through a small companion web app (see README). It talks only to Vetro on 127.0.0.1:8099 (to launch that app).\n// Plain ES5: older TVs run Node 4.4.\nvar fs = require('fs');\nvar path = require('path');\nvar http = require('http');\n\nvar MAX_TITLE = 40, MAX_MESSAGE = 200, MAX_QUEUE = 5, MAX_RECENT = 20, MAX_BODY = 8192;\nvar DEFAULT_SECONDS = 30, MIN_SECONDS = 5, MAX_SECONDS = 300, OPEN_EVERY_MS = 10000;\nvar APP_ID = /^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,127}$/;\nvar DEFAULT_APP = 'NotifCtr01.NotifCenter';\n\nmodule.exports = function (ctx) {\n    var queue = [];      // active notifications (memory only)\n    var recent = [];     // last ones sent, for the page (memory only)\n    var seq = 0;\n    var lastOpen = 0;\n\n    function appId() {\n        var c = ctx.config.get() || {};\n        return APP_ID.test(c.appId || '') ? c.appId : DEFAULT_APP;\n    }\n    function send(res, code, type, body) {\n        res.writeHead(code, { 'Content-Type': type, 'Cache-Control': 'no-store' });\n        res.end(body);\n    }\n    function sendJson(res, code, obj) { send(res, code, 'application/json; charset=utf-8', JSON.stringify(obj)); }\n    // The companion app can read the queue as a <script> when the TV's web runtime blocks cross-origin XHR.\n    function sendScript(res, obj) {\n        var json = JSON.stringify(obj).replace(/</g, '\\\\u003c');\n        json = json.split(String.fromCharCode(0x2028)).join('\\\\u2028').split(String.fromCharCode(0x2029)).join('\\\\u2029');\n        send(res, 200, 'application/javascript; charset=utf-8', 'window.__ncNotes&&window.__ncNotes(' + json + ');');\n    }\n    function wantsScript(req) { return /[?&]js=1(&|$)/.test(String(req.url || '')); }\n    function readBody(req, cb) {\n        var s = '';\n        req.on('data', function (d) { s += d; if (s.length > MAX_BODY) { req.destroy(); } });\n        req.on('end', function () { cb(s); });\n    }\n    function clean(text, max) {\n        return String(text == null ? '' : text).replace(/[\\x00-\\x1f]/g, ' ').slice(0, max).trim();\n    }\n    function prune() {\n        var now = Date.now();\n        queue = queue.filter(function (n) { return n.expires > now; });\n    }\n\n    // Asks Vetro to launch the companion app (at most once every 10 s).\n    function openApp() {\n        var now = Date.now();\n        if (now - lastOpen < OPEN_EVERY_MS) { return 'skipped (less than 10 s since the last launch)'; }\n        lastOpen = now;\n        var body = JSON.stringify({ appId: appId() });\n        try {\n            var rq = http.request({\n                host: '127.0.0.1', port: 8099, path: '/apps/launch', method: 'POST', timeout: 5000,\n                headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'Content-Length': Buffer.byteLength(body) }\n            }, function (r) { r.resume(); });\n            rq.on('error', function () { /* Vetro busy or app not installed */ });\n            rq.on('timeout', function () { rq.destroy(); });\n            rq.write(body);\n            rq.end();\n            return 'requested';\n        } catch (e) { return 'error'; }\n    }\n\n    function handleNotify(req, res) {\n        readBody(req, function (raw) {\n            var b;\n            try { b = JSON.parse(raw); } catch (e) { return sendJson(res, 400, { error: 'invalid JSON' }); }\n            b = b || {};\n            var message = clean(b.message, MAX_MESSAGE);\n            if (!message) { return sendJson(res, 400, { error: 'message is required' }); }\n            var secs = parseInt(b.seconds, 10);\n            if (!(secs >= MIN_SECONDS)) { secs = DEFAULT_SECONDS; }\n            if (secs > MAX_SECONDS) { secs = MAX_SECONDS; }\n            prune();\n            seq += 1;\n            var note = {\n                id: seq + '-' + Date.now().toString(36),\n                title: clean(b.title, MAX_TITLE),\n                message: message,\n                expires: Date.now() + secs * 1000\n            };\n            queue.push(note);\n            if (queue.length > MAX_QUEUE) { queue.shift(); }\n            recent.unshift({ id: note.id, title: note.title, message: note.message, at: Date.now() });\n            if (recent.length > MAX_RECENT) { recent.pop(); }\n            var opened = b.open === false ? 'not requested' : openApp();\n            sendJson(res, 200, { ok: true, id: note.id, open: opened });\n        });\n    }\n\n    function handleConfig(req, res) {\n        if (req.method === 'GET') { sendJson(res, 200, { appId: appId(), defaultAppId: DEFAULT_APP }); return true; }\n        readBody(req, function (raw) {\n            var b;\n            try { b = JSON.parse(raw); } catch (e) { return sendJson(res, 400, { error: 'invalid JSON' }); }\n            var id = b && b.appId;\n            if (!APP_ID.test(id || '')) { return sendJson(res, 400, { error: 'invalid appId' }); }\n            ctx.config.set({ appId: id });\n            sendJson(res, 200, { appId: id });\n        });\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    function sendFile(res, name, type) {\n        fs.readFile(path.join(__dirname, name), 'utf8', function (err, text) {\n            if (err) { return sendJson(res, 500, { error: name + ' is missing' }); }\n            send(res, 200, type, text);\n        });\n    }\n\n    return {\n        start: function () {},\n        stop: function () { queue = []; recent = []; },\n        status: function () { prune(); return { queued: queue.length, appId: appId() }; },\n        route: function (req, res, sub) {\n            sub = String(sub || '').split('?')[0].replace(/^\\/+|\\/+$/g, '');\n            if (sub === 'ui' && req.method === 'GET') { sendFile(res, 'ui.html', 'text/html; charset=utf-8'); return true; }\n            if (sub === 'nt.js' && req.method === 'GET') { sendFile(res, 'nt.js', 'application/javascript; charset=utf-8'); return true; }\n            if (sub === 'notify' && req.method === 'POST') { handleNotify(req, res); return true; }\n            if (sub === 'notifications' && req.method === 'GET') {\n                prune();\n                var now = Date.now();\n                var out = { notifications: queue.map(function (n) {\n                    return { id: n.id, title: n.title, message: n.message, seconds: Math.ceil((n.expires - now) / 1000) };\n                }) };\n                if (wantsScript(req)) { sendScript(res, out); } else { sendJson(res, 200, out); }\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (sub === 'recent' && req.method === 'GET') { sendJson(res, 200, { recent: recent }); return true; }\n            if (sub === 'config' && (req.method === 'GET' || req.method === 'POST')) { return handleConfig(req, res); }\n            return false;\n        }\n    };\n};\n","nt.js":"// Logic of the companion web app, served by the Shard (the app on the TV is only a thin loader, see README).\n// It runs inside the app, with the app's `notification` privilege. Plain ES5.\n(function () {\n  'use strict';\n  if (window.__ncLoaded) { return; }\n  window.__ncLoaded = true;\n\n  var BASES = ['http://127.0.0.1:8099'];\n  var NOTES_PATH = '/plugins/notification-center/api/notifications';\n  var SEEN_KEY = 'nc_seen', STAY_MS = 8000, WATCH_MS = 5000;\n  var logEl = document.getElementById('log');\n  var apiGood = null, busy = false;\n\n  function now() { var d = new Date(); function p(n) { return (n < 10 ? '0' : '') + n; } return p(d.getHours()) + ':' + p(d.getMinutes()) + ':' + p(d.getSeconds()); }\n  function log(cls, text) {\n    if (!logEl) { return; }\n    var line = document.createElement('div');\n    line.className = cls; line.textContent = now() + '  ' + text;\n    logEl.appendChild(line);\n    while (logEl.childNodes.length > 14) { logEl.removeChild(logEl.firstChild); }\n  }\n\n  function xhrGet(base, cb) {\n    var x = new XMLHttpRequest(), done = false;\n    function end(err, text) { if (!done) { done = true; cb(err, text); } }\n    try {\n      x.open('GET', base + NOTES_PATH); x.timeout = 4000;\n      x.onload = function () { if (x.status === 200) { end(null, x.responseText); } else { end('http ' + x.status); } };\n      x.onerror = function () { end('network'); };\n      x.ontimeout = function () { end('timeout'); };\n      x.send();\n    } catch (e) { end('blocked'); }\n  }\n  function scriptGet(base, cb) {\n    var s = document.createElement('script'), done = false, t;\n    function end(err, data) {\n      if (done) { return; }\n      done = true; clearTimeout(t); window.__ncNotes = undefined;\n      if (s.parentNode) { s.parentNode.removeChild(s); }\n      cb(err, data);\n    }\n    window.__ncNotes = function (d) { end(null, d); };\n    s.onerror = function () { end('network'); };\n    t = setTimeout(function () { end('timeout'); }, 5000);\n    s.src = base + NOTES_PATH + '?js=1&t=' + new Date().getTime();\n    (document.head || document.documentElement).appendChild(s);\n  }\n  function fetchQueue(done) {\n    var list = apiGood ? [apiGood] : BASES, i = 0, errors = [];\n    (function next() {\n      if (i >= list.length) { return done(errors.join('; ') || 'no address'); }\n      var base = list[i++];\n      xhrGet(base, function (err, text) {\n        if (!err) { try { apiGood = base; return done(null, JSON.parse(text).notifications || []); } catch (e) { err = 'json'; } }\n        scriptGet(base, function (err2, data) {\n          if (!err2) { apiGood = base; return done(null, (data && data.notifications) || []); }\n          errors.push(base + ' xhr:' + err + ' script:' + err2); next();\n        });\n      });\n    })();\n  }\n\n  function post(title, body, cb) {\n    try {\n      if (!window.Notification) { return cb('window.Notification is missing'); }\n      var show = function () { try { new Notification(title, { body: body }); cb(null); } catch (e) { cb('new Notification: ' + e.message); } };\n      if (Notification.permission === 'granted') { return show(); }\n      var r = Notification.requestPermission(function (p) { if (p === 'granted') { show(); } else { cb('permission ' + p); } });\n      if (r && r.then) { r.then(function (p) { if (p === 'granted') { show(); } else { cb('permission ' + p); } }); }\n    } catch (e) { cb(e.message); }\n  }\n\n  // On start, on resume and every few seconds while visible: post what is new, stay open while the banner shows, then exit.\n  function check(why) {\n    if (busy) { return; }\n    busy = true;\n    fetchQueue(function (err, list) {\n      if (err) { busy = false; return log('err', why + ': Shard unreachable (' + err + ')'); }\n      var seen = {}; try { seen = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(SEEN_KEY) || '{}'); } catch (e) { seen = {}; }\n      var fresh = list.filter(function (n) { return !seen[n.id]; });\n      if (!fresh.length) { busy = false; return log('inf', why + ': nothing new'); }\n      var pending = fresh.length;\n      fresh.forEach(function (n) {\n        seen[n.id] = 1;\n        post(n.title || 'Notification', n.message || '', function (e) {\n          log(e ? 'err' : 'ok', (n.title || 'Notification') + ': ' + (e || 'posted'));\n          pending -= 1;\n          if (pending) { return; }\n          try { localStorage.setItem(SEEN_KEY, JSON.stringify(seen)); } catch (x) { /* storage unavailable */ }\n          busy = false;\n          // Leaving too early hides the banner: stay open while it is on screen.\n          setTimeout(function () { try { tizen.application.getCurrentApplication().exit(); } catch (x) { /* not on a TV */ } }, STAY_MS);\n        });\n      });\n    });\n  }\n\n  check('start');\n  document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', function () { if (document.visibilityState === 'visible') { check('resume'); } });\n  setInterval(function () { if (document.visibilityState !== 'hidden') { check('watch'); } }, WATCH_MS);\n  document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {\n    if (e.keyCode === 10009 || e.keyCode === 27) { try { tizen.application.getCurrentApplication().exit(); } catch (x) { /* not on a TV */ } }\n  });\n})();\n","ui.html":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"dark light\">\n<title>Notification Center</title>\n<style>\n* { box-sizing: border-box; }\nbody { margin: 0; padding: 14px; font: 15px/1.4 system-ui, sans-serif; background: #12151c; color: #e8ecf2; }\nh1 { font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 12px; }\nh2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 18px 0 8px; color: #a9b8d6; }\n.card { background: #1b202b; border: 1px solid #2c3445; border-radius: 10px; padding: 12px; }\n.row { display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 8px; }\ninput, button { font: inherit; color: inherit; background: #232a38; border: 1px solid #3a4358; border-radius: 8px; padding: 7px 10px; }\ninput[type=text] { flex: 1; min-width: 160px; }\ninput[type=number] { width: 84px; }\nbutton { cursor: pointer; } button.primary { background: #2f6fed; border-color: #2f6fed; }\n.msg { min-height: 20px; font-size: 13px; color: #8a94a6; } .ok { color: #6fdc9a; } .err { color: #ff8a8a; }\nul { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; } li { padding: 6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid #2c3445; } li small { color: #8a94a6; }\ncode, pre { background: #0d1016; border-radius: 6px; padding: 2px 6px; font-size: 12px; }\npre { padding: 8px; overflow-x: auto; white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-all; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<h1>Notification Center</h1>\n\n<div class=\"card\">\n  <div class=\"row\"><input type=\"text\" id=\"title\" maxlength=\"40\" placeholder=\"Title (optional)\"></div>\n  <div class=\"row\"><input type=\"text\" id=\"message\" maxlength=\"200\" placeholder=\"Message\"></div>\n  <div class=\"row\">\n    <label>Seconds <input type=\"number\" id=\"secs\" min=\"5\" max=\"300\" value=\"30\"></label>\n    <label><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"open\" checked> Launch the companion app</label>\n    <button class=\"primary\" id=\"send\" type=\"button\">Send</button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"msg\" id=\"result\"></div>\n</div>\n\n<h2>Recently sent</h2>\n<div class=\"card\"><ul id=\"recent\"><li><small>Nothing yet.</small></li></ul><div class=\"row\" style=\"margin:8px 0 0\"><button id=\"refresh\" type=\"button\">Refresh</button></div></div>\n\n<h2>Companion app</h2>\n<div class=\"card\">\n  <div class=\"row\"><input type=\"text\" id=\"appid\" maxlength=\"128\" placeholder=\"App id\"><button id=\"save\" type=\"button\">Save</button></div>\n  <div class=\"msg\" id=\"cfg\"></div>\n  <div class=\"msg\">The app must be installed on the TV (see the README). The Shard only asks Vetro to launch it.</div>\n</div>\n\n<h2>Send from another device</h2>\n<div class=\"card\"><pre id=\"curl\"></pre></div>\n\n<script>\n(function () {\n  \"use strict\";\n  var $ = function (id) { return document.getElementById(id); };\n  function esc(s) { return String(s == null ? \"\" : s).replace(/[&<>\"']/g, function (c) { return { \"&\": \"&amp;\", \"<\": \"&lt;\", \">\": \"&gt;\", '\"': \"&quot;\", \"'\": \"&#39;\" }[c]; }); }\n  function say(el, text, cls) { el.textContent = text || \"\"; el.className = \"msg \" + (cls || \"\"); }\n  function api(path, body) {\n    var opt = body ? { method: \"POST\", headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" }, body: JSON.stringify(body) } : {};\n    return fetch(path, opt).then(function (r) { return r.json().then(function (j) { if (!r.ok) { throw new Error(j.error || \"error \" + r.status); } return j; }); });\n  }\n  function recent() {\n    api(\"recent\").then(function (d) {\n      $(\"recent\").innerHTML = d.recent.length ? d.recent.map(function (n) {\n        return \"<li><b>\" + esc(n.title || \"(no title)\") + \"</b> \" + esc(n.message) + \" <small>\" + new Date(n.at).toLocaleTimeString() + \"</small></li>\";\n      }).join(\"\") : \"<li><small>Nothing yet.</small></li>\";\n    }).catch(function (e) { say($(\"result\"), e.message, \"err\"); });\n  }\n  // The dashboard frame has no allow-forms: use buttons and the Enter key, not <form>.\n  $(\"send\").addEventListener(\"click\", function () {\n    say($(\"result\"), \"Sending...\");\n    api(\"notify\", { title: $(\"title\").value, message: $(\"message\").value, seconds: parseInt($(\"secs\").value, 10) || 30, open: $(\"open\").checked })\n      .then(function (r) { say($(\"result\"), \"Queued (launch: \" + r.open + \")\", \"ok\"); $(\"message\").value = \"\"; recent(); })\n      .catch(function (e) { say($(\"result\"), e.message, \"err\"); });\n  });\n  $(\"message\").addEventListener(\"keydown\", function (e) { if (e.key === \"Enter\") { $(\"send\").click(); } });\n  $(\"refresh\").addEventListener(\"click\", recent);\n  $(\"save\").addEventListener(\"click\", function () {\n    api(\"config\", { appId: $(\"appid\").value }).then(function (c) { say($(\"cfg\"), \"Saved: \" + c.appId, \"ok\"); }).catch(function (e) { say($(\"cfg\"), e.message, \"err\"); });\n  });\n  api(\"config\").then(function (c) { $(\"appid\").value = c.appId; });\n  $(\"curl\").textContent = 'curl -X POST http://<TV-IP>:8099/plugins/notification-center/api/notify \\\\\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\\\\n  -d \\'{\"title\":\"Oven\",\"message\":\"Dinner is ready\",\"seconds\":30}\\'';\n  recent();\n})();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}}
